			<div class="content" id="post-content-4474326">
									

<p>I certainly don't like made up techno-babble to justify that aren't even necessary for the narrative. And i find the all-too-convenient &quot;Note that explains it all&quot; found after Incident-XYZ-1337 a very cheap plot device.</p>
<p>Still&#8230; enough shenanigans with time to keep me entertained, and I'm used to enough crash-landings of 5000s that this one shines out as &quot;actually, it's not that bad&quot;. I don't know if you will think of it as a good or a bad review, but &quot;good enough&quot; is really just the way i can think of this in the context of the 5000 contest.</p>

